## The FHA Rules You Need to Know

### Occupancy Requirement

You must live in one of the units as your primary residence. This isn't optional—it's how you qualify for FHA's owner-occupant rates and down payment requirements.

You have 60 days after closing to move in and must stay for at least 1 year.

### Self-Sufficiency Test (3+ Unit Properties)

For properties with 3+ units, FHA requires the rental income to be sufficient to cover the mortgage. Specifically, 75% of the expected rental income is used in your debt-to-income calculation.

What this means: You can't buy a property that won't support itself. The numbers have to work.

### Reserve Requirements

For 3-4 unit properties, you'll need to have 3 months of PITI (Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance) in reserves after closing.

Example: If your PITI is $3,100/month, you need $9,300 in reserves.

This ensures you can cover payments if there's a vacancy.

## Why House Hacking Beats Traditional Investing

Traditional approach:
• Rent an apartment for $1,200/month
• Build zero equity
• After 10 years: $144,000 spent, $0 in assets

House hacking approach:
• Own a duplex, live in one unit for $1,000/month
• Tenant pays $1,500/month (more than covering your share)
• Build $500+/month in equity
• After 10 years: $120,000 out of pocket, $60,000+ in equity built, plus appreciation

The difference: You turned your housing expense into an investment.

## The Perfect First Investment

House hacking is ideal if you:

✓ Want to start investing with minimal down payment
✓ Want to learn landlording without the overwhelming responsibility of managing multiple properties
✓ Want to reduce your housing costs while building wealth
✓ Are willing to live with tenants for 1-3 years
✓ Want leverage and cash flow without being a professional investor

## Finding House Hacking Opportunities

The best house hacks in the Capital Region aren't always obvious. You need to know:
• Which neighborhoods are attracting tenants
• Which property types cash flow best (duplexes vs triplexes vs fourplexes)
• What rents the market will support
• How to model the financials correctly

